tual `#loop` representation with the\n    32\texact one-statement `Return(...) .Stmts` continuation and proves the returned\n    33\tvalue and complete frame-pop transition.\n    34\t\n    35\t`SPEC.correct-bracketing` loads the exact translated function body, performs\n    36\tnormal name lookup, argument evaluation, parameter binding, body execution,\n    37\treturn, and frame cleanup.  Its precondition is also `bracketInput(CS)`, and its\n    38\tpostcondition is the mathematical result above.\n    39\t\n    40\tThe three invariant obligations are discharged as follows:\n    41\t\n    42\t1. Empty suffix: fixed semantics exits the loop and the return expression\n    43\t   reduces to `V andBool B ==Int 0`, the base equation of `scanBrackets`.\n    44\t2. Nonempty suffix: fixed semantics binds the next one-character string,\n    45\t   executes the source branch and validity update, and returns to the same loop\n    46\t   configuration over the strict tail.  The recursive equation is exactly that\n    47\t   state transition.\n    48\t3. Entry: fixed semantics loads and calls the exact closure.  After the first\n    49\t   iteration establishes the `bracket` local, the proved loop theorem applies;\n    50\t   empty input exits directly.\n    51\t\n    52\t## Proof-extension inventory\n    53\t\n    54\t### `scanBrackets`\n    55\t\n    56\t- Class: definitional summary.\n    57\t- Semantic role: names the mathematical result; it does not rewrite an MPY\n    58\t  program term or replace execution.\n    59\t- Domain and coverage: all finite `IntSeq`, all integer balances, and both\n    60\t  Boolean flags.  `.IntSeq` and `iCons` are disjoint and exhaustive.  Recursive\n    61\t  calls use the strict tail.\n    62\t- Matched context and state footprint: none; it reads or changes no MPY cell.\n    63\t- Value influence: its Boolean is the loop theorem and entry theorem result.\n    64\t- Value justification: its base and step equations are the exact accumulator\n   